%% Four parties and the worker: the Operator Workspace, @ranza/reservations,
%% PostgreSQL, and apps/worker for the room a moved Guest leaves. The locks are
%% the global order of ADR 0038 — Unit, then the Property's day, then the Stay —
%% and a change that touches two Units takes both Unit locks in hashed order, so
%% two moves between the same rooms cannot deadlock.
%% OPEN (recommended in the decisions page): whether a move to another kind of
%% Unit keeps the booked price (recommended) or is re-priced like a booking.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor SM as Staff Member
  participant WS as Operator Workspace
  participant RS as @ranza/reservations
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  participant WK as apps/worker

  rect rgb(240, 248, 246)
  note over SM,PG: s1, change a booking that has not arrived
  SM->>WS: Change booking: new dates and/or Unit
  WS->>RS: previewChange(user, reservation, dates, Unit)
  RS->>PG: what holds those nights on that Unit, the price it would carry
  PG-->>RS: free, or the booking / Guest in house that holds them; the price
  RS-->>WS: preview (never a promise: the constraint decides on save)
  SM->>WS: Save, as previewed
  WS->>RS: amendBooking(user, reservation, change, previewed price)
  RS->>PG: lock 2 on old and new Unit (hashed order), lock 3 shared
  RS->>PG: update reservation dates / Unit (granted to amend only)
  PG->>PG: no-double-booking, one-occupancy, closed-day and sellability checks;<br/>price kept, or re-stamped for a new kind — compared with the preview
  RS->>PG: append reservation_changes; audit reservation.amended
  PG-->>RS: committed, or which rule refused it
  end

  rect rgb(246, 244, 240)
  note over SM,PG: s2 and s3, an in-house Guest
  SM->>WS: Extend / shorten, or Move with a reason
  WS->>RS: changeDeparture(user, stay, departs, preview) or moveGuest(user, stay, Unit, reason)
  RS->>PG: lock 2 (Units), lock 3 shared, lock 1 (Stay)
  RS->>PG: update stay ends_on or Unit, and its Reservation's, in one transaction
  PG->>PG: one-occupancy (ADR 0033), the new Unit in service and ready (a move),<br/>no night already spent is re-dated or re-roomed
  RS->>PG: append reservation_changes; outbox stay.moved; audit stay.*
  end

  rect rgb(240, 244, 250)
  note over WK,PG: the room a moved Guest left
  WK->>PG: stay.moved -> mark the old Unit dirty (as stay.checked_out does)
  end
